  "host_adaptations": [
    "Complete original IA32 procedures independently reassembled and normalized instruction-equal before ELF64 ABI adaptation.",
    "Source cdecl32 argument slots expanded to host8-byte stack slots; source local pointers remain low32 addresses on an isolated low stack.",
    "Original function-token words remain unmodified in tree keys and16-byte snapshots; only the F48 indirect control transfer is bridged to an explicitly typed provider.",
    "Separate reviewed node32, snapshot16 and variable allocators; monotonically increasing logical IDs with no reuse in the bounded512-allocation profile. Fresh variable bytes use deterministic A5 allocator policy; original F51 writes only its first8 bytes.",
    "Original F42 subtraction wrap/order, duplicate-right insertion, F45 predecessor deletion, F46 subtree snapshot traversal and F54 signed highest-state selection run unchanged.",
    "Readonly normalized module definitions provide the actual pointer-load structure for F54 cleanup and F51 variable sizes; no original VM program execution is claimed.",
    "Host callbacks normalize pointers to arena slots and logical variables; mutable registry actions invoke actual original F44/F45/F50; temporary callback snapshots are not externally mutable.",
    "Semantically undefined EAX returns of source void workers are excluded; compare results and task allocation pointer/packed-handle distinction remain explicit."
  ],
  "scope": "Bounded whole F42/F43/F44/F45/F46/F48/F49/F50/F51/F54/F55/F56 with explicit event callback/F53/F41/F52 providers. No full F41 VM, F47 body, F52 argument interpreter, Main or APK claim."
